wh40k-class-specialization-overseer-formation-doctrine-name = Doctrine of Iron Will
wh40k-class-specialization-overseer-formation-doctrine-description = Commands and direct buffs for eligible players within ten tiles.

wh40k-class-skill-overseer-formation-doctrine-01-name = Right to Command
wh40k-class-skill-overseer-formation-doctrine-01-description = Unlocks the command stance and ten-tile recipient rule: all nearby players when ungrouped, or only party members when grouped.
wh40k-class-skill-overseer-formation-doctrine-02-name = Shoulder to Shoulder
wh40k-class-skill-overseer-formation-doctrine-02-description = Recipients near the Overseer gain moderate knockback and stamina-damage resistance. Multiple commanders do not stack it.
wh40k-class-skill-overseer-formation-doctrine-03-name = Priority Target
wh40k-class-skill-overseer-formation-doctrine-03-description = Marks a visible hostile NPC for current recipients. Their first controlled shot or strike gains accuracy, not raw damage.
wh40k-class-skill-overseer-formation-doctrine-04-name = “Take Cover” Order
wh40k-class-skill-overseer-formation-doctrine-04-description = Briefly orders allies into cover, improving resistance to frontal fire only while actually in cover.
wh40k-class-skill-overseer-formation-doctrine-05-name = Formation Step
wh40k-class-skill-overseer-formation-doctrine-05-description = Out of combat, recipients following a visible Overseer move slightly faster in formation. Attacking, firing, or leaving ten tiles ends it.
wh40k-class-skill-overseer-formation-doctrine-06-name = Crisp Reload
wh40k-class-skill-overseer-formation-doctrine-06-description = The first reload after a command mark is harder to interrupt and starts slightly faster. No ammunition is created.
wh40k-class-skill-overseer-formation-doctrine-07-name = Rally Signal
wh40k-class-skill-overseer-formation-doctrine-07-description = Places a formation point visible to recipients. Reaching it briefly improves stamina recovery without healing or teleportation.
wh40k-class-skill-overseer-formation-doctrine-08-name = Coordinated Fire
wh40k-class-skill-overseer-formation-doctrine-08-description = When two recipients attack a marked NPC from different positions, their first hits build less spread or attack delay.
wh40k-class-skill-overseer-formation-doctrine-09-name = Banner of Order
wh40k-class-skill-overseer-formation-doctrine-09-description = Deploys a formation beacon from a real consumable. It shows command range but provides no cover, weapon, or endless buffs.
wh40k-class-skill-overseer-formation-doctrine-10-name = Fire Rotation
wh40k-class-skill-overseer-formation-doctrine-10-description = Briefly speeds transitions between firing and reloading for nearby allies, with an internal cooldown preventing another such order.
wh40k-class-skill-overseer-formation-doctrine-11-name = Do Not Falter
wh40k-class-skill-overseer-formation-doctrine-11-description = Shortens each nearby ally's first minor slow or action disruption. It does not remove heavy stuns, critical condition, or medical injuries.
wh40k-class-skill-overseer-formation-doctrine-12-name = “Advance” Order
wh40k-class-skill-overseer-formation-doctrine-12-description = Gives current recipients a short controlled movement impulse toward a visible point; firing or collision ends it immediately.
wh40k-class-skill-overseer-formation-doctrine-13-name = All-Round Defense
wh40k-class-skill-overseer-formation-doctrine-13-description = Two or more nearby recipients facing different directions gain a small frontal defense bonus. The group is not invulnerable.
wh40k-class-skill-overseer-formation-doctrine-14-name = Coordinated Aid
wh40k-class-skill-overseer-formation-doctrine-14-description = A recipient begins healing, reloading, or helping another recipient faster. The interaction and real items remain required.
wh40k-class-skill-overseer-formation-doctrine-15-name = Order in Chaos
wh40k-class-skill-overseer-formation-doctrine-15-description = For a few seconds, one selected command category—fire, defense, or movement—survives a small range break. Other categories gain nothing.
wh40k-class-skill-overseer-formation-doctrine-16-name = Retaliatory Formation
wh40k-class-skill-overseer-formation-doctrine-16-description = When a recipient is hit, the nearest other recipient briefly gains accuracy on their first response against the visible source.
wh40k-class-skill-overseer-formation-doctrine-17-name = Veteran's Voice
wh40k-class-skill-overseer-formation-doctrine-17-description = Restores a little stamina and clears a minor combat disruption from current recipients. It does not heal damage, blood, toxins, or prone allies.
wh40k-class-skill-overseer-formation-doctrine-18-name = Spearhead
wh40k-class-skill-overseer-formation-doctrine-18-description = During Advance, the first ally to reach the point briefly resists knockback; each order has only one spearhead.
wh40k-class-skill-overseer-formation-doctrine-19-name = Full Formation
wh40k-class-skill-overseer-formation-doctrine-19-description = Briefly combines weakened fire, defense, and movement effects for all recipients. It has a long cooldown and cannot overlap another full command.
wh40k-class-skill-overseer-formation-doctrine-20-name = Heart of the Formation
wh40k-class-skill-overseer-formation-doctrine-20-description = Final node: improves only the currently active formation order through one capped modifier. Orders never stack or persist between bodies.
